    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe can use place value strategies to multiply any whole number by [MATH: 10.]\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's use our understanding of place value to solve the following multiplication problem:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4 \\times 10]\n\nContent:\nRemember that [MATH: 4 \\times 10] means \"[MATH: 4] groups of [MATH: 10.]\" Therefore,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4 \u00d7 10|=; 10 + 10 + 10 + 10_(\u23df)_(4times)|=; 4tens + 0ones|=; 40|.]\n\nContent:\nThe same computation can be explained visually as follows:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/5ad9a6ed55aade2c0000960caae03e6c]\n\nContent:\nSo, we conclude that\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4\\times 10 = 40.]\n\nContent:\nWe can use the same strategy to multiply two-digit numbers by [MATH: 10,] too. Let's see an example.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Multiplying a Number by Ten\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: 35 \\times 10.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that [MATH: 35 \\times 10] means [MATH: 35] groups of [MATH: 10.] Therefore,\n\n[MATH: 35 \u00d7 10|=; 10 + 10 + \u22ef + 10_(\u23df)_(35times)|=; 35tens + 0ones|=; 3hundreds + 5tens + 0ones|=; 350|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate the following product. Express your answer as a whole number.[MATH: 3 \u00d7 10 =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 3 \u00d7 10 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3]\nb. [MATH: 300]\nc. [MATH: 10]\nd. [MATH: 100]\ne. [MATH: 30]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Multiplying a Number by One Hundred\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 17 \\times 100?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that [MATH: 17 \\times 100] means [MATH: 17] groups of [MATH: 100.] Therefore,\n[MATH: 17 \u00d7 100|=; 100 + 100 + \u22ef + 100_(\u23df)_(17times)|=; 17hundreds + 0tens + 0ones|=; 1thousands + 7hundreds + 0tens + 0ones|=; 1, 700|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 2 \u00d7 100 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 20]\nb. [MATH: 200]\nc. [MATH: 400]\nd. [MATH: 2, 000]\ne. [MATH: 1, 000]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate the following product. Express your answer as a whole number.[MATH: 25 \u00d7 100 =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Multiplying a Number by One Thousand\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind [MATH: 79 \\times 1,000.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nRemember that [MATH: 79 \\times 1,000] means [MATH: 79] groups of [MATH: 1,000.] Therefore,\n[MATH: 79 \u00d7 1, 000|=; 1, 000 + 1, 000 + \u22ef + 1, 000_(\u23df)_(79times)|=; 79thousands + 0hundreds + 0tens + 0ones|=; 7ten-thousands + 9thousands + 0hundreds + 0tens + 0ones|=; 79, 000|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 9 \u00d7 1, 000 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 9, 100]\nb. [MATH: 90, 000]\nc. [MATH: 910]\nd. [MATH: 900]\ne. [MATH: 9, 000]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 18 \u00d7 1, 000 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 1, 800]\nb. [MATH: 180, 000]\nc. [MATH: 180]\nd. [MATH: 18, 000]\ne. [MATH: 10, 000]"
